{"annotations":{"openWorldHint":false,"readOnlyHint":true},"description":"One metric's daily values as CSV, oldest first. Without from/to it returns the last 365 days; pass from (and to) as yyyy-MM-dd for other ranges. Use list_metrics for the ids. Long-term context for Bitcoin holders, not trading signals. Show the closing \"Source:\" line to the user.","execution":{"taskSupport":"forbidden"},"inputSchema":{"$schema":"http://json-schema.org/draft-07/schema#","properties":{"from":{"description":"First UTC day, yyyy-MM-dd.","pattern":"^\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}$","type":"string"},"id":{"description":"The metric id, e.g. bitcoin-mvrv-ratio.","enum":["bitcoin-mvrv-z-score","bitcoin-price","bitcoin-mayer-multiple","bitcoin-200-week-moving-average","bitcoin-hodl-waves","bitcoin-hashrate","bitcoin-mining-difficulty","bitcoin-puell-multiple","bitcoin-block-interval","bitcoin-block-size","bitcoin-transactions-per-day","bitcoin-mvrv-ratio","bitcoin-realized-price","bitcoin-percent-supply-in-profit","bitcoin-realized-cap","bitcoin-realized-profit-loss"],"type":"string"},"to":{"description":"Last UTC day, yyyy-MM-dd.","pattern":"^\\d{4}-\\d{2}-\\d{2}$","type":"string"}},"required":["id"],"type":"object"},"name":"get_metric","title":"Get a metric"}
